        {
          "id": "2020-iab-adtech-part2",
          "year": 2020,
          "title": "Inzicht in Adtech PART 2",
          "summary": "In the second IAB Nederland adtech webinar, moderated by Tim Geenen of the IAB Nederland board, Rob van Eijk of the Future of Privacy Forum moves from mechanics to consent. He revisits his measurements of third-party calls on European newspaper sites. Audience measurement under the Dutch analytics exemption, he explains, needs a processor agreement behind it. He walks through the GDPR conditions for valid consent, the Planet49 ruling, and the open question of cookie walls, and explains how a complaint to a regulator differs from a tip. He then reviews real sites with developer tools. He finds requests to third parties before any choice, separate consent across one company's brand sites, and refusals that take several clicks. His main lesson is that withdrawing consent must be as easy as giving it. In between he points to de-identification techniques such as differential privacy as a promising direction.",
