        {
          "id": "2020-understanding-adtech",
          "year": 2020,
          "title": "Understanding Adtech",
          "summary": "Christy Harris and Rob van Eijk of the Future of Privacy Forum give a webinar on online advertising in the Understanding Digital Data Flows series. Harris covers the basics: advertisers and publishers, first and third parties in the browser, cookies and pixels, supply-side and demand-side platforms, data management platforms and ad servers, and how companies recognise users across sites and devices. Van Eijk explains how browsers work, takes apart a display ad, and demonstrates fingerprinting. His graph measurements separate real-time bidding networks on newspaper sites in 27 European countries. He compares default tracking protections in Chrome, Firefox, and Safari. He then describes the end of third-party cookies: Google's Privacy Sandbox proposals such as FLoC, discussions in W3C groups, and the IAB's Project Rearc.",
